{"event_type":"review","id":"4ccfb75b32cc421b877f1b03288d1a6b28481c5f673dbcef4287e240b33b2774","occurred_at":"2026-11-05T20:44:35Z","payload":{"artifacts":[{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/2f354c4e346b50af672f537b74ae413f96160b97407503dcc0b65654546a7836","sha256":"2f354c4e346b50af672f537b74ae413f96160b97407503dcc0b65654546a7836"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/c120b6c004b1d89c7e748a68b5fbefe7f3a0c3677f655ba1ee8dc758b70c7e29","sha256":"c120b6c004b1d89c7e748a68b5fbefe7f3a0c3677f655ba1ee8dc758b70c7e29"},{"kind":"git-bundle","location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/4121a99c22ffa550134e1c5e9ab30cc8c52a37819ce574c6c440a566ece7ac85","sha256":"4121a99c22ffa550134e1c5e9ab30cc8c52a37819ce574c6c440a566ece7ac85"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/ead3760ec1d55a01752549c285fd446f9aae8bc40cc79a925d7bb9ed52cf9c54","sha256":"ead3760ec1d55a01752549c285fd446f9aae8bc40cc79a925d7bb9ed52cf9c54"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/f060dd5e7dddadfd09160aa01a38dbccdad49b7112da525f2404bc91975c9218","sha256":"f060dd5e7dddadfd09160aa01a38dbccdad49b7112da525f2404bc91975c9218"}],"attempt_id":"eb38b82d57a939b4560c660c8d4468f7507594a5a38fd1e35cc92ae5918bebd8:0:1","base":"57d9d3d149f15270ce7888b4c5871a0e1174d19a","completion":{"errors":[],"exit_code":0,"scope_verified":true,"skipped":false,"terminal":true},"findings":[{"anchor_status":"unverified","blob":"4062000000a5b0127c13dc60c8a4b45be0e2585a","body":"**A missing `.cq/review/<branch>` folder returns a raw ENOENT error instead of the documented guidance.**\n\n`readdir(folder)` throws ENOENT when `review.run` has never run on the branch. The outer catch (Line 2006) turns that error into `needs-human` with the raw error text. The friendly message at Line 1922 (`no findings record; run review.run or pass --record`) never appears. The README (Lines 10-11) documents that guidance. Treat ENOENT as an empty list.\n\n<details>\n<summary>Proposed fix</summary>\n\n```diff\n-                  const files = (await readdir(folder))\n+                  const files = (\n+                    await readdir(folder).catch((error: NodeJS.ErrnoException) => {\n+                      if (error.code === 'ENOENT') return [] as string[];\n+                      throw error;\n+                    })\n+                  )\n                     .filter((name) => /^\\d+\\.json$/.test(name))\n```\n</details>","id":"fa74caa6deef7741dd58c8503e6fe5ab457cda72f58a89a8e91884b6f50b93b8","intervals":[],"path":"src/ops/review/address.ts","severity":"minor","source_id":null,"status":"untriaged","title":"A missing `.cq/review/<branch>` folder returns a raw ENOENT error instead of the documented guidance."},{"anchor_status":"unverified","blob":"4062000000a5b0127c13dc60c8a4b45be0e2585a","body":"**Refuse stale refresh after bookkeeping is fingerprinted.**\n\nA later address round can call `runReviewLoop` again. If stale worktree removal fails, `onWorktreeStaleRefresh` deletes receipt-owned files, and `onWorktreeCreated` retires the receipt. The shared fingerprint map and receipt state remain unchanged. The next bookkeeping access can mark the run tampered because a fingerprinted file no longer exists. The receipt check is also stale and would reject once reached.\n\nUse the existing strict refusal when bookkeeping already contains fingerprints:\n\n<details>\n<summary>Suggested fix</summary>\n\n```diff\n-                  if (!persistedBookkeeping) return false;\n+                  if (!persistedBookkeeping || bookkeeping.size > 0) return false;\n```\n\n</details>","id":"7be4781cc382dcea2cb95eee5a3918e5a038bf263d33d26f367bea9840453ae3","intervals":[],"path":"src/ops/review/address.ts","severity":"major","source_id":null,"status":"untriaged","title":"Refuse stale refresh after bookkeeping is fingerprinted."}],"head":"396b4485dd1c1465f76378246c6497916bcff0e2","head_tree":"013c2fa4bf520f2358e9d1367a3d73c21ab4fb44","input_scope":[{"blob":"72794fded0e770a8ab2e8c611cbe24b2754e638f","intervals":[[1,268]],"path":"src/ops/review/README.md"},{"blob":"4062000000a5b0127c13dc60c8a4b45be0e2585a","intervals":[[1,2017]],"path":"src/ops/review/address.ts"},{"blob":"634c765d910e8d8e6df4fefcd49ab8469fa556d8","intervals":[[1,237]],"path":"src/ops/review/internal/addressBookkeeping.ts"}],"job_id":"eb38b82d57a939b4560c660c8d4468f7507594a5a38fd1e35cc92ae5918bebd8:0","outcome":"completed","paths":[{"baseline":{"method":"projection","reason":"residual uncovered lines"},"blob":"72794fded0e770a8ab2e8c611cbe24b2754e638f","disposition":"included","mode":"100644","path":"src/ops/review/README.md","reason":"bounded verified input"},{"baseline":{"method":"projection","reason":"residual uncovered lines"},"blob":"4062000000a5b0127c13dc60c8a4b45be0e2585a","disposition":"included","mode":"100644","path":"src/ops/review/address.ts","reason":"bounded verified input"},{"baseline":{"method":"projection","reason":"residual uncovered lines"},"blob":"634c765d910e8d8e6df4fefcd49ab8469fa556d8","disposition":"included","mode":"100644","path":"src/ops/review/internal/addressBookkeeping.ts","reason":"bounded verified input"}],"policy_digest":"3aee477168e1da8e2aa232a98e80747d98da8f26f54f2a27e0c62d13e349d4b1","repo":"camerontaylor/cq-toolkit","requested_scope":[{"blob":"72794fded0e770a8ab2e8c611cbe24b2754e638f","intervals":[[1,268]],"path":"src/ops/review/README.md"},{"blob":"4062000000a5b0127c13dc60c8a4b45be0e2585a","intervals":[[1,2017]],"path":"src/ops/review/address.ts"},{"blob":"634c765d910e8d8e6df4fefcd49ab8469fa556d8","intervals":[[1,237]],"path":"src/ops/review/internal/addressBookkeeping.ts"}],"reviewed_scope":[{"blob":"72794fded0e770a8ab2e8c611cbe24b2754e638f","intervals":[[1,268]],"path":"src/ops/review/README.md"},{"blob":"4062000000a5b0127c13dc60c8a4b45be0e2585a","intervals":[[1,2017]],"path":"src/ops/review/address.ts"},{"blob":"634c765d910e8d8e6df4fefcd49ab8469fa556d8","int